{"label":"paddle-2026-11-08","title":"Your paddle, Nov 8 \u00b7 calm","window":{"start":"2026-11-08T20:19:30.225000Z","end":"2026-11-08T21:15:46Z"},"observed":{"rating":"calm","quality":"calm water in the lee of the revetment; very windy (offshore west) at the outer edge of the track","by":"paddler","notes":"Afternoon paddle from the Diversey Harbor launch, north through the harbor and out the mouth, south along the Fullerton revetment to off Theater on the Lake, and back. Very windy at the track's outer (east) edge, so we hugged the shoreline: the whole lake stretch stays within ~50-100 m of the wall. The water stayed calm (fine ripples, no whitecaps or swell) even where the wind was strong, since an offshore wind had no fetch to build waves there; the risk was being blown out, not chop.","photos":["2:29 PM CST exiting Diversey Harbor at the mouth, looking south along the Fullerton revetment to the skyline: fine ripples and cat's paws, no whitecaps, cloudless sky, pale green-turquoise water translucent near the board (photo in spotchecks/photos/2026-11-08-north-ave-1429.jpg)"],"spots":[{"lat":41.9275,"lon":-87.6281,"r_m":200,"rating":"calm","note":"outer edge of the track ~100 m off the revetment: very windy offshore west wind, gusty, water still mostly ripples; turned back toward the wall to avoid being blown out"}]},"track":{"name":"Nov 8 paddle","start":"2026-11-08T20:19:30.225000Z","source":"GPX (route, speed and a GPS roughness index; heart rate not stored)","fields":["t_s","x_m","y_m","speed_ms","unused","bump"],"pts":[[0,-414.4,4953.3,0.66,null,0.29],[6,-406.9,4961.1,2.2,null,0.261],[11,-399.1,4965.8,1.63,null,0.164],[17,-393.8,4973.5,1.65,null,0.134],[22,-390.8,4983.8,2.06,null,0.14],[27,-391.0,4994.2,2.54,null,0.123],[33,-393.7,5006.2,1.84,null,0.105],[38,-394.7,5017.0,2.37,null,0.136],[43,-392.7,5028.0,2.22,null,0.188],[48,-390.4,5035.6,1.5,null,0.269],[53,-388.9,5041.0,1.08,null,0.289],[58,-386.2,5044.5,0.98,null,0.18],[64,-387.3,5053.2,1.54,null,0.187],