rstates an offshore wind past the first ~50-100 m. The sea state was calm throughout (0.06 m forecast, fine ripples seen): with offshore wind the hazard is drift, not waves, so a calm-looking photo near the wall doesn't contradict the no-go.","GPS roughness: bump on the lake stretch (median 0.065 while moving, p95 0.22) was the same as inside Diversey Harbor (0.066, p95 0.16): calm, a little short of glass (Oct 21 glass: median 0.05, p95 ~0.17).","clarity: pale green, translucent water at the harbor mouth (~1-3 FNU by eye) agreed with Sentinel-2's 2.0 FNU at Diversey from Oct 26, the newest clear view."]}